<title>PERU: IADB approves $45.6 mln agricultural loan for Peru.</title>
<headline>IADB approves $45.6 mln agricultural loan for Peru.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Inter-American Development Bank (IADB) said Wednesday it had approved a $45.6 million loan to Peru to boost agricultural output and exports.</p>
<p>The money will help a fund a government agricultural program whose total cost is $76 million.</p>
<p>The Washington-based IADB said in a faxed statement the loan was payable over 20 years, with five years' grace, at a variable interest rate currently at 6.9 percent.</p>
<p>((-- Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
